We can solve this problem by using the Law of Sines for triangles $BAD$ and $DAE$:
\begin{align*}
\frac{\sin x}{\overline{AB}} &= \frac{\sin (x + y)}{\overline{BD}} \\
\frac{\sin y}{\overline{AD}} &= \frac{\sin (y + z)}{\overline{DE}} = \frac{\sin (x + y)}{\overline{EC}} \\
\end{align*}
Since $BD = DE = EC$, we can find $EC$:
\begin{align*}
\overline{EC} &= \overline{BD} = \overline{DE} \\
