\begin{document}

\maketitle

Let girls\_total denote the total number of miles run by a girl at the point when the coach orders new equipment.

First, we need to find when the girl's total mileage surpasses the boy's mileage each day.
Let the difference between the girl's and boy's total mileage at the end of day t be
\begin{align*}
 girls\_total(t) - boys\_total(t) & = 3 * t + 1 - 5 * t \\
                                         & = -2 * t + 3.
\end{align*}

Now we have a linear inequality,

\begin{align*}
 -2 * t + 3 > 0,
\end{align*}

or
\begin{align*}
