\frac{2}{a} + \frac{1}{b} &= \frac{2}{1-2b} + \frac{1}{b} \\
&= \frac{2b + 1}{b(1 - 2b)}
\end{align*}
To find the minimum value of the above expression, we'll use calculus to analyze the behavior of the function. However, for simplicity, we can get a lower bound by finding the value that makes the numerator equal to zero:
